e sources with different formats and schemas. Here's what was accomplished:\n\n### Key Results\n- **4 unique users** merged from 6 total records across 3 sources\n- **3 conflicts** detected and resolved using source priority\n- All field mappings applied correctly\n- Dates normalized to YYYY-MM-DD format\n- Data types correctly set (user_id as integer)\n\n### Merged Dataset (`/app/merged_users.parquet`)\nContains 4 rows with columns:\n- `user_id` (integer)\n- `name` (string)\n- `email` (string)\n- `created_date` (YYYY-MM-DD format)\n- `status` (string)\n\n### Conflict Resolution\nWhen user 101 appeared in all three sources with different values, the highest-priority source (A) was selected:\n- **Email**: Selected `john@a.com` from source_a (conflicted with source_b and source_c)\n- **Created date**: Selected `2024-01-15` from source_a (conflicted with different dates in other sources)\n- **Name**: Selected `John Doe` from source_a (conflicted with abbreviated name in source_c)\n\n### Output Files\n- **`/app/merged_users.parquet`** - Final merged dataset (4 users)\n- **`/app/conflicts.json`** - Detailed conflict report with all values and selections\n\nAll success criteria have been met. The merge prioritizes source_a > source_b > source_c and properly tracks all conflicts in the generated report.","ttft_ms":2233,"type":"result","duration_ms":57046,"uuid":"057b2b72-a608-43a0-b0e9-3b480648ced5","ttft_stream_ms":914,"time_to_request_ms":87,"queued_turn_count":0}
